What this repository contains, and what derives from what.

1. Written for this repository: MIT (LICENSE)
   README.md, docs/, the overlay READMEs, every compose file under overlays/*/engine/, overlays/g4/bench/,
   overlays/sq/pipespec/, multinode/, tools/apply-overlays.sh and tools/stage0-4bit/. The compose files follow
   the form of cebeuq's recipe. tools/stage0-4bit/stage0_4bit.py calls the compressed-tensors library
   (https://github.com/vllm-project/compressed-tensors, Apache-2.0) and copies none of its code.

2. Modified vLLM source files: Apache License 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)
   Every file under overlays/*/patches/vllm/ but one is a modified copy of a vLLM source file
   (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm) as shipped in the engine image the recipe pins,
   lazymio/vllm-backport@sha256:2627d2a97e7f539b99ac98f511c589f5f520d3fc5630b195aca7f6ef865ead4e, built from
   https://github.com/wtdcode/vllm-backport at 29e66dad461b11caae6039f510eaa7913f9dfb19. Each file keeps its
   header "SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0" and "SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM
   project". Several start from cebeuq's patched copy of the vLLM file in
   https://github.com/cebeuq/glm53-cmp170hx-recipe (commit 31c0934958a8b0892b6de139e37d2bfe18926ae4; that
   repository is MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 cebeuq, LICENSES/MIT-cebeuq.txt). vLLM ships no NOTICE file.

   The one exception is sq/sq_pipespec_core.py: it derives from cebeuq's own PipeSpec module
